# Lua style

Follow `docs/style/lua.md`. Match the current file’s indent (games: 4 spaces; many `functions/` files: tabs).

```lua
-- ✅ dual load + baseURL
local baseURL = shared.sempatpanick_baseURL
assert(type(baseURL) == "string" and #baseURL > 0, "[sempatpanick] baseURL not set")

-- ❌ require-only (breaks executor HttpGet)
local mod = require("../../functions/player/character")
```

- Keep require-then-HttpGet loaders; strip UTF-8 BOM; `loadstring or load`.
- Always check Lua’s **200 local** limit before adding locals to a game file. `do` does not reset it; wrap large tabs in `local function createXTab()`. Details: `docs/style/lua.md`.
- Sempat/Rayfield window title: `sempatpanick | <Name>`. Persist flags via `flagsPrefix`, not ad-hoc names.
- Do not fork `tabs/rayfield` logic into a game file or into `tabs/windui` beyond the wrap.
- Do not edit `rayfield_library.lua` / `windui_library.lua` for a single-game feature.
